    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5503790/graduate-research-assistant": {
      "title": "Graduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "Graduate Research Assistant Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-02092 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - School of Travel Industry Management Opening Date 10/02/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: 0000GA11 Description Title: Graduate Assistant Position Number: 0000GA11 Hiring Unit: Shidler College of Business / School of Travel Industry Management Location: University of Manoa, Honolulu HI Date Posted: 10/02/2026 Closing Date: Continuous recruitment until the position is filled; first review on 10/19/2026 Salary Information: $31,524/yr Monthly Type: 11-month Full Time/Part Time: Part Time - Full Time Equivalency: 50% Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Funding: Federal Other Conditions: (if applicable) Renewal dependent on performance, departmental needs and/or funding availability. Duties and Responsibilities Conduct literature reviews relevant to the research projects. Collect, process, integrate, and analyze large-scale transportation datasets. Develop machine learning and artificial intelligence methods for pedestrian volume estimation. Assist in developing databases, data processing pipelines, and online visualization tools. Assist in preparing technical reports, journal manuscripts, conference papers, and research presentations. Participate in project meetings. Communicate and coordinate with project partners and stakeholders. Perform other research-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Currently enrolled (or admitted) as a graduate student at the University of Hawai?i at Manoa. Bachelor's degree in Engineering, Computer Science, Data Science, Geography, Statistics, or a related field. Familiarity with artificial intelligence, machine learning, big data analytics, databases, and computer programming. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to prepare technical reports and research manuscripts. Ability to organize tasks and work independently as well as collaboratively. Desirable Qualifications Experience with transportation data collection and analysis or intelligent transportation systems. Experience with machine learning, deep learning, or artificial intelligence. Experience with Python, R, SQL, GIS (ArcGIS/QGIS), or related programming and data analysis tools. Experience with scientific writing and conference or journal publications. Valid driver's license. Master's degree in a related field To Apply: Click on the \"Apply\" button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach required documents. Applicant must submit the following: Cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications; Resume or CV; Names and contact information (telephone number and email addresses) of 3 professional references; and Official transcripts Note: If you have not applied for a position before using NeoGov, you will need to create an account. Inquiries: Dr. Xiaofeng Li, Xiaofeng.li@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
