    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5132315/instructor-i2-applied-computing-pmcs-0082794": {
      "title": "Instructor (I2) Applied Computing (PMCS) #0082794",
      "description": "Instructor (I2) Applied Computing (PMCS) #0082794 Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Permanent Job Number 2025-02308 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Natural Sciences - ICS Opening Date 11/04/2025 Position Number: 0082794 Description Title: Instructor (I2) Applied Computing (PMCS) Position Number: 0082794 Hiring Unit: University of Hawai’i at Manoa, College of Natural Science, Information & Computer Science Location: University of Hawai’i at Manoa Date Posted: November 4, 2025 Closing Date: Continuous; First review will begin January 15, 2026 until filled Salary Information: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Monthly Type: 9 Month Tenure Track: Non-tenure Full Time/Part Time: Full-Time Temporary/Permanent: Permanent Other Conditions: Subject to position clearance and availability of funds. First review of applicants will begin January 15, 2026 with continuous recruitment until position is filled. 9-month renewal dependent upon performance and availability of funds. Duties and Responsibilities: Help develop and implement the professional program courses. Teach one or more courses in the ICS Department’s Professional AI Program, including Applied Computing Industry Seminar, Applied Computing Fundamentals, Data Science and AI, and Practical Problem Solving with Algorithms. Oversee graduate teaching assistants and advising graduate students. Mentor students for capstone Internship projects. Network with industry and public sectors to identify projects. Network with industry and public-sector partners to identify and secure relevant project opportunities for students. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Computer Science, Data Science or in a closely related field from a college or university of recognized standing. Ability to contribute to curriculum and course development in applied AI/Data Science. Strong written and oral communication skills. Ability to teach effectively and to direct group discussions. Prior teaching experience. Experience with modern AI frameworks such as PyTorch and the Hugging Face ecosystem, as well as familiarity with tools used in Generative AI workflows (e.g., LangChain, vector databases). Desirable Qualifications: PhD in Computer Science or in a closely related field from a college or university of recognized standing. At least 2 years of professional experience in applied computing, AI or data science. Evidence of at least 5 years of professional experience in AI or Data Science. Strong commitment to professional graduate AI education. Experience teaching computer sciences courses for people without a computer science background. Experience in teaching in multiple modalities (online, face to face, hybrid, etc). To Apply: Click on the “Apply” button on the top right corner of the screen and attach the required documents. Applicants must submit (1) cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications, (2) resume, (3) names and contact information of 3 professional references and (4) copies of transcripts with confidential identifiable information (i.e. social security number, birth date, etc.) redacted are acceptable, however, official transcripts will be required at the time of hire. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Inquiries: Guylaine Poisson (guylaine@hawaii.edu), Department Chair, Information and Computer Sciences EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/4898540/instructor-marine-biology-0084043t": {
      "title": "Instructor (Marine Biology - 0084043T)",
      "description": "Instructor (Marine Biology - 0084043T) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Temporary Job Number 2025-00818 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Natural Sciences - School of Life Sciences Opening Date 04/07/2025 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: 0084043T Description Title: Instructor Position Number: 0084043T Location: M a noa Campus Date Posted: April 07, 2025 Closing Date: Continuous until filled, first review of application begins 5 /01 /2025 Salary Info: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Monthly Type: 9-Month Tenure Track: Non-Tenure Full Time/Part Time: Full-Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Funding: General Funds Other Conditions: The School of Life Sciences (SoLS), College of Natural Sciences, University of Hawai‘i at Manoa (Honolulu, Hawai'i) invites applicants for the position of Instructor in the Marine Biology undergraduate program. With over 600 students, Marine Biology is one of the largest majors at UHM. This is a temporary, non-tenure track, full-time, 9-month, faculty appointment, to begin January2 , 202 6 , subject to position clearance, availability of funds, and program needs. Review of applications will begin on May 01 , 2025 and will continue until the position is filled. The University of Hawai'i at Manoa (UHM) is a Native Hawaiian place of learning and a Carnegie Research 1 University with a strong emphasis on research and undergraduate and graduate education. Our vision is to be locally and globally recognized as a premier student-centered and community-serving university. For more information on the Manoa Strategic Plan and additional information about Manoa’s Strategic Vision as a Native Hawaiian place of learning, visit: https://manoa.hawaii.edu/strategicplan/ . For more information on the school, please visit: https://manoa.hawaii.edu/lifesciences/ . Duties: Teaching 12-credits (or equivalent) per semester, including Biology of the Invertebrates (BIOL 485+485L), Marine Ecology and Evolution (BIOL 301+301L), Advanced Topics in Marine Biology (BIOL 404) and other undergraduate classes in the Marine Biology program. Participate in SoLS committees and events as appropriate. Perform related tasks as assigned Minimum Qualifications: A Master’s degree in Marine Biology, or related discipline, from a college or university of recognized standing, with the major work in the field in which the instructional assignment is made or duties performed Evidence of ability to teach effectively and to direct group discussions Professionalism in meeting and conferring with others Desirable qualifications include : Ph.D. in Marine Biology, or related discipline, (or closely related discipline), A proven track record of effective course instruction in lower and upper-division marine biology courses at the university level, Experience teaching high enrollment (>60) lecture courses with multiple lab sections, Experience teaching students of varied backgrounds To Apply: Applicants must submit one single PDF file that contains: Cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications Curriculum vitae, including teaching history, a list of prior scholarly achievements and a list of publications and presentations Names and contact information (including email addresses and phone numbers) of three professional references. At least one of these references should be your current supervisor or an acceptable substitute with close knowledge of your current academic program and/or teaching experience. Relevant course evaluations and sample syllabi Transcripts from all institutions of higher education. Statement summarizing your teaching interests and how they intersect with instructional activities at an R1 institution, and the courses listed under duties above. Official transcripts with proof of degree conferred will be required upon hire. Inquiries: Megan Porter, mlporter@hawaii.edu Continuous recruitment. Review of applications will begin May 01, 2025 , and continue until the position is filled. Applications received before that date will be given priority. EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5497847/it-manager-0080018": {
      "title": "IT Manager (0080018)",
      "description": "IT Manager (0080018) Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Permanent Job Number 2026-02059 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - Office of the Vice Provost for Enrollment Management Opening Date 09/28/2026 Closing Date 10/19/2026 11:59 PM Hawaii Position Number: 0080018 Description Title: IT Manager Position Number: 0080018 Hiring Unit: Office of the Vice Provost for Enrollment Management Location: Manoa Date Posted: September 28, 2026 Closing Date: October 19, 2026 @ 11:59 PM Band: C Salary : salary schedules and placement information Additional Salary Information: PBC, minimum $6,876/month Full Time/Part Time: Full-time Month: 11-month Temporary/Permanent: Permanent Duties and Responsibilities PLAN AND ORGANIZE *Serves as the senior subject matter expert and advisor to the Vice Provost for Enrollment Management on enterprise student systems, systems integration, technology strategy, and institutional business process alignment. *Provides strategic oversight, coordination, and stewardship of enterprise systems supporting enrollment management and student success at the UH Manoa campus. *Develops and maintains long-range systems strategies that align Office of Enrollment Management technology capabilities with institutional priorities and operational needs. *Identifies emerging institutional needs, systems risks, operational inefficiencies, and opportunities for improvement and develops recommendations that support long-term institutional objectives in enrollment management. *Coordinates organization of and discussion with campus stakeholders, technical teams, functional offices, and administrative leadership regarding enterprise systems, business processes, operational requirements, and institutional priorities within the Office of Enrollment Management. *Prepares implementation plans and identifies major tasks, milestones, dependencies, and resource requirements associated with Office of Enrollment Management enterprise systems initiatives. *Serves on task forces, committees, governance groups, and special projects representing Enrollment Management and providing expertise regarding enterprise systems and institutional process integration. MANAGE, DIRECT, DEVELOP, AND COORDINATE *Directs, leads, develops, and executes initiatives that enhance the student experience and improve institutional effectiveness in enrollment management through the strategic use of enterprise technologies and integrated business processes. *Identifies, recommends, and facilitates solutions that reduce barriers to student enrollment, persistence, progression, and graduation. *Serves as the primary liaison between Enrollment Management, Information Technology Services (ITS), UH System stakeholders, vendors, and campus leadership regarding enterprise enrollment management systems initiatives, priorities, requirements, and enhancements. *Provides strategic oversight and coordination for the integration and alignment of enterprise platforms supporting enrollment management, student success, curriculum management, advising, reporting, communications, and institutional planning. *Sets strategic and operational priorities for Enrollment Management Information Technology initiatives in alignment with institutional goals and enterprise technology strategies. *Directs and leads the planning, development, implementation, and continuous improvement of new Enrollment Management initiatives and supporting technologies. *Directs, manages, motivates, utilizes, and supervises Enrollment Management Information Technology personnel and UH student employees. *Serves as mentor and professional resource for subordinate staff by providing guidance, development opportunities, performance feedback, and challenging assignments. *Establishes team development procedures, methodologies, standards, and guidelines to promote operational effectiveness, consistency, innovation, and sustainability. *Develops recommendations regarding systems governance practices, operational standards, business processes, and institutional guardrails that promote consistency, compliance, and effective service delivery. *Makes decisions regarding the application and modification of existing and emerging technologies, systems hardware, software, integrations, and business processes that significantly impact Enrollment Management operations and campus stakeholders. *Defines project roles and responsibilities; establishes priorities; allocates resources; and adjusts project plans in response to changing institutional needs and operational requirements. *Defines project scope, objectives, deliverables, timelines, and implementation strategies; develops recommendations regarding business process improvements, service enhancements, and customer experience improvements. *Coordinates and assists ITS with proof-of-concept evaluations, testing activities, implementation planning, and adoption of enterprise technologies targeted for use by Enrollment Management and other institutional stakeholders. *Coordinates and assists ITS with enterprise system upgrades, testing, validation, implementation, and change management activities associated with systems such as Banner, reporting environments, document management platforms, and related enterprise applications. *Communicates directly with stakeholders to identify, evaluate, and resolve complex systems issues and serves as liaison among technical teams, functional offices, and institutional leadership. SYSTEMS ANALYSIS, REQUIREMENTS DEFINITION, CONCEPTUAL AND DETAILED DESIGN *Analyzes complex institutional requirements and evaluates the operational, fiscal, compliance, academic, and student-success impacts of proposed systems changes, enhancements, and initiatives. *Formulates and defines overall system scope, design, functionality, and integration requirements; gathers and analyzes complex user, operational, and institutional requirements; and develops effective and sustainable solutions. *Evaluates business processes and recommends process redesign, systems integration, automation, and service improvement opportunities. *Determines technical feasibility of proposed system modifications, enhancements, integrations, and implementation approaches. *Develops recommendations and solutions to unprecedented and highly complex systems issues requiring consideration of multiple institutional priorities and competing interests. *Develops standards and methodologies that promote efficiency, consistency, maintainability, and effective use of institutional resources. *Develops software testing procedures; designs and coordinates system testing; evaluates test results; determines operational readiness; and oversees quality assurance activities. *Evaluates emerging technologies, industry trends, and evolving institutional needs and develops recommendations regarding adoption, modernization, and long-term systems sustainability. *Provides expert analysis and recommendations supporting enrollment management, financial aid administration, reporting, and student success initiatives. *Continuously monitor and lead initiatives to enhance system reliability, security, and operational efficiency. Supervise and mentor IT staff to assure that administrative directives and industry best practices are understood and followed. *Follows and implements directives and guidance related to best practices from University of Hawai'i System Information Technology Services. *Ensures the consistent adoption, implementation, and enforcement of recommendations issued through University of Hawai'i System Information Technology Services. *Keeps abreast of recommendations issued through University of Hawai'i System Information Technology Services and takes timely action as needed. Other Duties As Assigned *Denotes essential duties Minimum Qualifications Possession of a pertinent baccalaureate educational degree in Management Information Systems, Information and Computer Science (ICS), Information Systems, Business Analytics, Data Analytics, Public Administration, Higher Education Administration, or a related field, and seven (7) years of progressively responsible professional experience involving systems analysis, enterprise systems integration, business process improvement, enterprise applications, information technology leadership, data and reporting environments, or implementation and support of complex institutional systems, of which two (2) years of the experience must have been comparable in scope and complexity to the next lower pay band in the University of Hawai'i broadband system; or any equivalent combination of education and/or professional work experience which provides the required education, knowledge, skills and abilities as indicated. Advanced and comprehensive knowledge and understanding of a wide range of developing and emerging information technology concepts, principles and methodologies of systems analysis, design, and implementation. Comprehensive knowledge and understanding of a wide range of interactive and integrated technology, systems, hardware and software associated with systems analysis, design, and implementation. Demonstrated ability to understand problems from a broad interactive perspective and use reasoning to discern underlying principles and issues when problem solving, and apply creative thinking to resolve problems in new and unprecedented approaches. Proven ability to comprehend, interpret and implement administrative directives and guidance to ensure IT operations align with organizational standards and industry best practices. Demonstrated written and verbal competence in presenting ideas, concepts and models clearly using persuasion and negotiation to build consensus and cooperation. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with internal and external organizations, groups, team leaders and members, and individuals. For supervisory work, demonstrated ability to lead subordinates, manage work priorities and projects, and manage employee relations. Comprehensive knowledge and demonstrated ability to develop and revise systems plans, design documents, implementation plans, training materials, and to conduct user group sessions and related interviews. Comprehensive knowledge and demonstrated ability in one or more Database Management Systems (DBMS) such as Oracle, SQL Server, PostgreSQL, MySQL, or comparable enterprise database environments. Comprehensive knowledge and demonstrated ability in systems development, systems integration, business process analysis, project implementation methodologies, and related techniques. Comprehensive knowledge of enterprise student information systems, enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems, customer relationship management (CRM) systems, or comparable institutional platforms. Strong understanding of IT service management, cybersecurity principles, risk management, and compliance requirements. Demonstrated experience implementing and maintaining IT best practices, standards, and governance. Ability to work a variable work schedule and work outside normally scheduled work hours including day, night, weekend, and/or holiday hours, as directed. Desirable Qualifications Considerable working knowledge of enterprise student information systems in large public post-secondary institutions or comparable organizations. Considerable working knowledge of Banner, DegreeWorks, Salesforce, EAB Navigate, Acalog, Curriculog, or comparable higher education enterprise platforms. Considerable working knowledge of data reporting, analytics, business intelligence, and institutional decision-support environments. Considerable working knowledge of state and federal rules, regulations, practices, policies, and procedures relating to confidentiality of student records, including the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) of 1974. Considerable working knowledge of financial aid systems, student records systems, enrollment management operations, or related higher education administrative functions. Demonstrated ability to lead complex cross-functional initiatives involving multiple stakeholders, business units, and technology platforms. To Apply: Click on the “Apply” button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach required documents. Applicant must submit the following: Resume Cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications Names of 3 professional references Official transcripts* * Must submit an official undergraduate college transcript with verification of degree awarded. Unofficial web-based transcripts or other course and grade reports (e.g. STAR report for UHM) will not be accepted. Copies of official educational transcripts will be accepted but an original transcript must be submitted if selected prior to hiring. Confidential information must be redacted (i.e. social security number, date of birth, etc.). Note: If you have not applied for a position before using NeoGov, you will need to create an account. Inquiries: Nikki Chun; nkchun@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. In accordance with Article 10 of the unit 08 collective bargaining agreement, bargaining unit members receive priority consideration for APT job vacancies. As a result, external or non BU 08 applicants may not be considered for some APT vacancies. BU 08 members with re-employment rights or priority status are responsible for informing the hiring unit of their status. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
