    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/3126106/lecturer-american-studies": {
      "title": "Lecturer (American Studies)",
      "description": "Lecturer (American Studies) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2021-00461 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - Department of American Studies Opening Date 06/21/2021 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description Title: Lecturer (American Studies) Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages, and Letters, Department of American Studies Location: Manoa Date Posted: June 21, 2021 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum salary: $2053 per credit hour Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in lecturer pool beginning Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027. Positions are part-time, temporary, non-tenure, and contingent upon course offerings, sufficient student enrollment, position clearance, and availability of funds. Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate or graduate American Studies courses or equivalent. Other related duties, including preparing course syllabus, grading, maintaining weekly office hours. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in American Studies (or applicable field). Desirable Qualifications PhD in American Studies (or related field) or doctoral work in American Studies (or related field). Knowledge in appropriate field as evidenced by coursework. Prior relevant university teaching experience in the field. Training in and/or experience with online teaching To Apply: Email cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications, curriculum vitae, two letters of recommendation, and transcripts (copies are acceptable; however original transcripts will be required at time of hire) to amstuh@hawaii.edu. Application materials will not be returned. Inquiries: Brandy McDougall, Department Chair, amstchair@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai’i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ . Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai’i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai’i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ . Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
