      "description": "Lecturer (Japanese) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2018-01038 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - Department of East Asian Language & Literatures Opening Date 04/05/2016 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description Title: Lecturer (Japanese) Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages & Letters, Dept. of East Asian Languages and Literatures Location: Manoa Date Posted: April 05, 2016 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum $2,053 per credit hour; commensurate with qualifications and experience. Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in department adjunct lecturer pool for Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027. Mainly part-time employment, contingent on approval to fill, course offerings (ranging from 3 to 12 credits), position clearance, availability of funds, and sufficient enrollment. Appointments offered on a semester basis. Duties and Responsibilities To teach basic language skill courses in the target language. Minimum Qualifications MA in the target language or related discipline required. High-level fluency in the target language and English. Desirable Qualifications College-level classroom experience in teaching Japanese language. To Apply: Submit cover letter of interest for the position, CV, transcripts (copies are acceptable; official transcripts will be required at time of hire) and 3 letters of recommendation to the address below. Address: East Asian Languages and Literatures 1890 East-West Road, Moore 382 Honolulu, HI 96822 Inquiries: Dr. Mary Shin Kim, Chair; 808-956-8940; eall@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai’i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.e